IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-art02-making`
IMPORT `je21-art04-08-effects`

-- je21-tests-art04-08-effects: tests for Articles 4 to 8.
-- The expected values were written by hand from the text of each Article before the module was run.

§ `Articles 4 to 8 -- tests`

§§ `Names for the readings (the first of each pair is the default)`

`L5 adopted` MEANS `made by the States means adopted by the States Assembly, as Article 2(1)(a) and 2(3)(a) put it, so it covers Laws, Regulations and Acts`
`L5 Law only` MEANS `made by the States means a Law only`
`L9 expiry counts` MEANS `Article 5 applies to legislation that has expired or otherwise ceased to have effect, whether or not other legislation repealed it`
`L9 repeal only` MEANS `Article 5 applies only where Jersey legislation repeals other Jersey legislation`
`L10 displaced too` MEANS `a contrary provision that displaces paragraph (2) displaces paragraph (3) too, which speaks only of things mentioned in paragraph (2)`
`L10 unqualified` MEANS `paragraph (3) has no "unless" limb and applies even where paragraph (2) is displaced`
`L12 exhaustive` MEANS `an applicability clause is exhaustive, so what lies outside it is not within the Article`
`L12 names only` MEANS `an applicability clause only names what it includes, so the Law does not say whether the Article reaches what lies outside it`

§§ `4(1) The powers Article 4 covers`

#ASSERT `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` TRUE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` `a power to establish an entity` TRUE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` `a power to make an appointment` TRUE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` `a power to give a notice or document` TRUE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` `a power to prescribe a form` TRUE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` `a power to do any other thing for the purposes of the legislation` TRUE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` `a power of none of these kinds` TRUE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` `a power to make an appointment` FALSE `L12 exhaustive`

-- Fork L12: a power outside the clause (one a UK Act gives, or one of none of the listed kinds) is not covered on the first reading, and the Law does not say on the second.
-- A power inside the clause is covered on both.
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` TRUE `L12 names only`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` `a power to do any other thing for the purposes of the legislation` TRUE `L12 names only`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` FALSE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` FALSE `L12 names only` BECAUSE "Article 4(1) says Article 4 applies to Jersey legislation that confers power to do the things it lists, and the Law does not say whether Article 4 applies to any other power"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` `a power of none of these kinds` TRUE `L12 names only` BECAUSE "Article 4(1) says Article 4 applies to Jersey legislation that confers power to do the things it lists, and the Law does not say whether Article 4 applies to any other power"

§§ `4(2) Exercise before the legislation is in force`

#ASSERT `Article 4(2): Article 4 permits the power to be exercised before the legislation is in force` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT `Article 4(2): Article 4 permits the power to be exercised before the legislation is in force` `a power to prescribe a form` TRUE TRUE FALSE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 4(2): Article 4 permits the power to be exercised before the legislation is in force` `a power to prescribe a form` TRUE TRUE TRUE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 4(2): Article 4 permits the power to be exercised before the legislation is in force` `a power to prescribe a form` TRUE FALSE FALSE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 4(2): Article 4 permits the power to be exercised before the legislation is in force` `a power of none of these kinds` TRUE TRUE FALSE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 4(2): Article 4 permits the power to be exercised before the legislation is in force` `a power to prescribe a form` FALSE TRUE FALSE `L12 exhaustive`

-- Fork L12: the reading reaches Article 4(2) through Article 4(1).
#ASSERT `Article 4(2): Article 4 permits the power to be exercised before the legislation is in force` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE `L12 names only`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 4(2): Article 4 permits the power to be exercised before the legislation is in force` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 4(2): Article 4 permits the power to be exercised before the legislation is in force` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `L12 names only` BECAUSE "Article 4(1) says Article 4 applies to Jersey legislation that confers power to do the things it lists, and the Law does not say whether Article 4 applies to any other power"

§§ `4(3) Subordinate legislation not in force before the power`

#ASSERT NOT `Article 4(3): bringing the subordinate legislation into force on that day is not barred` (YMD 2022 3 9) (YMD 2022 3 10)
#ASSERT `Article 4(3): bringing the subordinate legislation into force on that day is not barred` (YMD 2022 3 10) (YMD 2022 3 10)
#ASSERT `Article 4(3): bringing the subordinate legislation into force on that day is not barred` (YMD 2022 3 11) (YMD 2022 3 10)

§§ `5(1) and 5(5) When Article 5 applies`

#ASSERT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `L9 repeal only` `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` FALSE TRUE `it was repealed` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` TRUE FALSE `it was repealed` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` FALSE TRUE `it expired` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` FALSE TRUE `it expired` `L9 repeal only` `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` FALSE TRUE `it otherwise ceased to have effect` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` FALSE TRUE `it otherwise ceased to have effect` `L9 repeal only` `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` TRUE TRUE `it has not ended` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` FALSE FALSE `it expired` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 exhaustive`

-- Fork L12: a repeal by something that is not Jersey legislation, or of something that is not Jersey legislation, is outside the clause.
-- It is not within Article 5 on the first reading, and the Law does not say on the second.
-- Legislation that has not ended has nothing to apply to, and is FALSE on both.
#ASSERT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 names only`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` FALSE TRUE `it was repealed` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` FALSE TRUE `it was repealed` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 names only` BECAUSE "Article 5(1) says Article 5 applies where Jersey legislation repeals other Jersey legislation or a provision of it, and the Law does not say whether Article 5 applies to anything else"
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` TRUE FALSE `it was repealed` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` TRUE FALSE `it was repealed` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 names only` BECAUSE "Article 5(1) says Article 5 applies where Jersey legislation repeals other Jersey legislation or a provision of it, and the Law does not say whether Article 5 applies to anything else"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` TRUE FALSE `it expired` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 names only` BECAUSE "Article 5(1) says Article 5 applies where Jersey legislation repeals other Jersey legislation or a provision of it, and the Law does not say whether Article 5 applies to anything else"
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` TRUE TRUE `it has not ended` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 names only`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` FALSE TRUE `it expired` `L9 repeal only` `L12 names only`
-- The reading reaches Articles 5(2), 5(3) and 5(4) through the argument "Article 5 applies".
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` (`Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` FALSE TRUE `it was repealed` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 names only`) FALSE BECAUSE "Article 5(1) says Article 5 applies where Jersey legislation repeals other Jersey legislation or a provision of it, and the Law does not say whether Article 5 applies to anything else"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 5(3): the proceeding may be brought or the penalty imposed as if the legislation had not been repealed` (`Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` FALSE TRUE `it was repealed` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 names only`) TRUE FALSE `L10 displaced too` BECAUSE "Article 5(1) says Article 5 applies where Jersey legislation repeals other Jersey legislation or a provision of it, and the Law does not say whether Article 5 applies to anything else"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 5(4): the repeal does not revive the thing` `legislation that was repealed` (`Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` FALSE TRUE `it was repealed` `L9 expiry counts` `L12 names only`) FALSE BECAUSE "Article 5(1) says Article 5 applies where Jersey legislation repeals other Jersey legislation or a provision of it, and the Law does not say whether Article 5 applies to anything else"

§§ `5(2) What a repeal does not affect`

#ASSERT `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `the validity, invalidity, effect or consequences of anything done or suffered under the repealed legislation` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `an amendment of legislation made by the repealed legislation` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `the previous operation of the repealed legislation, or anything done or permitted under it` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy that relates to a right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability under it` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred for an offence committed, or a breach, before the repeal` TRUE FALSE
-- A contrary provision displaces each of them.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `the validity, invalidity, effect or consequences of anything done or suffered under the repealed legislation` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `an amendment of legislation made by the repealed legislation` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `the previous operation of the repealed legislation, or anything done or permitted under it` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy that relates to a right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability under it` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred for an offence committed, or a breach, before the repeal` TRUE TRUE
-- Article 5 does not apply: nothing is preserved by it.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE FALSE

§§ `5(3) Proceedings and penalties continue`

#ASSERT `Article 5(3): the proceeding may be brought or the penalty imposed as if the legislation had not been repealed` TRUE TRUE FALSE `L10 displaced too`
#ASSERT `Article 5(3): the proceeding may be brought or the penalty imposed as if the legislation had not been repealed` TRUE TRUE FALSE `L10 unqualified`
-- A contrary provision: the readings differ.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(3): the proceeding may be brought or the penalty imposed as if the legislation had not been repealed` TRUE TRUE TRUE `L10 displaced too`
#ASSERT `Article 5(3): the proceeding may be brought or the penalty imposed as if the legislation had not been repealed` TRUE TRUE TRUE `L10 unqualified`
-- Not a thing mentioned in paragraph (2), or Article 5 not applying: no reading helps.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(3): the proceeding may be brought or the penalty imposed as if the legislation had not been repealed` TRUE FALSE FALSE `L10 displaced too`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(3): the proceeding may be brought or the penalty imposed as if the legislation had not been repealed` TRUE FALSE TRUE `L10 unqualified`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(3): the proceeding may be brought or the penalty imposed as if the legislation had not been repealed` FALSE TRUE FALSE `L10 displaced too`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(3): the proceeding may be brought or the penalty imposed as if the legislation had not been repealed` FALSE TRUE TRUE `L10 unqualified`

§§ `5(4) What a repeal does not revive`

#ASSERT `Article 5(4): the repeal does not revive the thing` `legislation that was repealed` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 5(4): the repeal does not revive the thing` `a rule of law that had been abolished` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 5(4): the repeal does not revive the thing` `any other thing not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(4): the repeal does not revive the thing` `legislation that was repealed` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(4): the repeal does not revive the thing` `a rule of law that had been abolished` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(4): the repeal does not revive the thing` `any other thing not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(4): the repeal does not revive the thing` `legislation that was repealed` FALSE FALSE

§§ `6 Repeal and re-enactment`

#ASSERT `Article 6: the reference to the repealed provision is construed as a reference to the re-enacted provision` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 6: the reference to the repealed provision is construed as a reference to the re-enacted provision` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 6: the reference to the repealed provision is construed as a reference to the re-enacted provision` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 6: the reference to the repealed provision is construed as a reference to the re-enacted provision` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 6: the reference to the repealed provision is construed as a reference to the re-enacted provision` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 6: the reference to the repealed provision is construed as a reference to the re-enacted provision` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

§§ `7 Amendment of subordinate legislation by a Law, etc`

-- 7(1): an amendment by a Law.
#ASSERT `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `an Order` `a Law` `L5 adopted`
#ASSERT `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `Regulations` `a Law` `L5 adopted`
#ASSERT `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` `a Law` `L5 Law only`
-- 7(2): subordinate legislation not made by the States, amended by Regulations.
#ASSERT `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `an Order` `Regulations` `L5 adopted`
#ASSERT `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `an Order` `Triennial Regulations` `L5 adopted`
#ASSERT `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `an Order` `Regulations` `L5 Law only`
-- Regulations amended by Regulations: the readings of "made by the States" (L5) differ.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `Regulations` `Regulations` `L5 adopted` BECAUSE "Article 7 says nothing of an amendment by Regulations of subordinate legislation made by the States"
#ASSERT `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `Regulations` `Regulations` `L5 Law only`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `Triennial Regulations` `Triennial Regulations` `L5 adopted` BECAUSE "Article 7 says nothing of an amendment by Regulations of subordinate legislation made by the States"
-- Neither paragraph reaches these.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `an Order` `an Order` `L5 adopted` BECAUSE "Article 7 says nothing of an amendment by anything but a Law, or, for subordinate legislation not made by the States, Regulations"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `Regulations` `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` `L5 adopted` BECAUSE "Article 7 says nothing of an amendment by anything but a Law, or, for subordinate legislation not made by the States, Regulations"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `a Law` `a Law` `L5 adopted` BECAUSE "Article 7 is about the amendment of Jersey subordinate legislation, and a Law is not subordinate legislation"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `UK extended legislation` `a Law` `L5 adopted` BECAUSE "Article 7 is about the amendment of Jersey subordinate legislation, and UK extended legislation is not Jersey subordinate legislation"

§§ `8 Overlap of relevant periods`

-- Each period begins on the day lodged and ends on the day made, both inside it.
-- Overlap by some days.
#ASSERT `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 2 15) (YMD 2022 4 20)
-- The first ends the day before the second begins: no day in common.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 2 14) (YMD 2022 2 15) (YMD 2022 4 20)
-- The first ends on the day the second begins: that one day is in both.
#ASSERT `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 2 15) (YMD 2022 2 15) (YMD 2022 4 20)
-- The second ends on the day the first begins.
#ASSERT `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2022 2 15) (YMD 2022 4 20) (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 2 15)
-- The second ends the day before the first begins.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2022 2 15) (YMD 2022 4 20) (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 2 14)
-- One inside the other, either way round.
#ASSERT `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2022 1 1) (YMD 2022 12 31) (YMD 2022 5 1) (YMD 2022 5 2)
#ASSERT `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2022 5 1) (YMD 2022 5 2) (YMD 2022 1 1) (YMD 2022 12 31)
-- Two Laws each lodged and made on one day.
#ASSERT `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2022 5 1) (YMD 2022 5 1) (YMD 2022 5 1) (YMD 2022 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2022 5 1) (YMD 2022 5 1) (YMD 2022 5 2) (YMD 2022 5 2)
-- Wholly apart.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2021 3 1) (YMD 2022 1 1) (YMD 2022 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2022 1 1) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2021 3 1)
-- A year end and a leap day inside a period do not disturb it.
#ASSERT `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2023 12 1) (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 3 5)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2023 12 1) (YMD 2024 2 28) (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 3 5)
-- A Law made before it was lodged has no relevant period.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 2 15) (YMD 2022 4 20) BECAUSE "a Law made before it was lodged has no relevant period under Article 8(2)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 4 20) (YMD 2022 2 15) BECAUSE "a Law made before it was lodged has no relevant period under Article 8(2)"

§§ `8(1) The power`

#ASSERT `Article 8(1): Article 8 gives the States power to amend the Law consequentially on the other Law` (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 2 15) (YMD 2022 4 20)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8(1): Article 8 gives the States power to amend the Law consequentially on the other Law` (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 2 14) (YMD 2022 2 15) (YMD 2022 4 20)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8(1): Article 8 gives the States power to amend the Law consequentially on the other Law` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 2 15) (YMD 2022 4 20) BECAUSE "a Law made before it was lodged has no relevant period under Article 8(2)"
